course: dictionary
lesson: 1999
title: Conceited and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A conceited person thinks far too well of themselves. In the story, Toad sings «The world has held great Heroes… but never a name to go down to fame compared with that of Toad!» He is singing about himself, so he must be very proud of himself. That is what conceited means.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. The barge-woman says, «I thought you must be a humbug all along, from the conceited way you talked.» The way Toad talked about himself shows that conceited means too proud, and boasting about it.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «What a conceited and heedless ass!» If you put "too proud of yourself" in place of conceited, the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: Conceited means too proud of yourself.
fact: The noun is conceit, which means a very high opinion of yourself.
fact: Opposites of conceited are modest and humble.
fact: Conceited can describe a way of talking or behaving, as in «the conceited way you talked».
fact: In a story, a conceited character often boasts and then gets a lesson, as Toad does in The Wind in the Willows.
exercise: «What a conceited and heedless ass!» What does conceited mean here? | Quiet and shy | Kind and generous to everyone | Very tired and sleepy | *Too proud of yourself
exercise: Toad sings songs about how wonderful he is. Which word means the opposite of conceited? | *Modest | Clever | Boastful | Cheerful
exercise: The robins «perched and hopped on them in their perky conceited way, just as if they had done it themselves». Why does the author say the robins are conceited? | Because they are hungry and cold | Because they sing very badly | *Because they act as if they had built the snow-castles themselves | Because they are sad and quiet
test: Which is the best meaning of conceited? | Very frightened | *Too proud of yourself | Too tired to move | Covered in snow
test: Find the word in this sentence that means the opposite of conceited: «Ella was humble when she won, and she thanked everyone.» | *humble | won | thanked | everyone
exam: Toad sings about his own name going down to fame. Why is Toad conceited? | He is shy and quiet | He is lost in the wood | *He is far too proud of himself and boasts about his own name | He is helping his friends
